# Each v3_final_completed_* evaluation output directory mixes small
# aggregate tables (pcr/, statistics/, by_model_dataset/,
# answers/final_answer_summary.csv -- a few hundred KB total, the actual
# paper-facing outputs) with large raw per-row/per-example dumps
# (answers/final_answer_predictions.jsonl, evidence/*.csv, audits/*) that
# are fully reproducible from traces + code via `analysis.cli` and don't
# belong in git. Only the aggregates are un-ignored below, per directory
# (a directory not listed here -- e.g. a future all-models run -- needs the
# same block added once it's generated).
!results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/
results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/*
!results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/pcr/
!results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/statistics/
!results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/by_model_dataset/
!results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/answers/
results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/answers/*
!results/evaluation/v3_final_completed_qwen_llama_20260914/answers/final_answer_summary.csv

# analysis/canonical/ is otherwise a small, fully-tracked code+writeup
# package, but a handful of raw per-row audit outputs (43k-65k rows each,
# 1.8M-6.2M) and one provenance zip bundle ended up sitting alongside it.
# All are reproducible on demand from results/ via their generating script
# (canonical_completion.py, retrieval_equivalence.py,
# final_gap_audit/direct_exit_content_audit.py) and aren't needed to verify
# any claim in the small aggregate tables that ARE tracked -- ignore only
# these specific files, not the directories they live in.
analysis/canonical/canonical_run_level_completion.csv
analysis/canonical/retrieval_equivalence_by_pair.csv
analysis/canonical/final_gap_audit/direct_exit_content_audit.csv
analysis/canonical/final_gap_audit/chapter3_final_gap_audit_bundle.zip

# Archived/superseded code and result directories -- kept on local disk for
# provenance, but not tracked in git at all (large raw data plus superseded
# code that would otherwise clutter the publishable tree).
archive/

# Chapter-3-methodology audit trail: git-status/inventory snapshots and zip
# bundles used locally to verify each reorganization pass was behavior-
# preserving, and as the restore source for PRELAUNCH_REPORT.json /
# v3_final_production_matrix.json if a --mode generate/validate re-run
# overwrites them (see PUBLISHING.md, "Provenance preservation"). Audit
# trail, not a paper deliverable -- kept on local disk, not git-tracked.
chapter3_methodology_audit/

# Claude Code internal metadata, and other local agent-tool config dirs
# unrelated to the paper (empty placeholders some tools create on disk).
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/

# Cluster-only directories unrelated to this project's ODR/attack line of work
adaptive-rag/
self-rag/
scripts/

# >100 MB (GitHub per-file limit); regenerable from traces via the results-bundle generator
gemma_gptoss_results_bundle/data/answer_run_level.csv
